-- The sign of a composite permutation is the product of the signs: a
-- permutation with no inversions is the identity, an inversion yields an
-- adjacent descent, exchanging at a descent removes exactly one inversion,
-- and induction on the number of inversions does the rest
-- Part of Cumulus, the Grace17 mathematics library.
-- Copyright (c) 2026 Grant Passmore.
